WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.802
Text cleaning is a pipeline, not one magic function.

00:00:03.802 --> 00:00:06.177
First inspect the raw value.

00:00:06.177 --> 00:00:09.322
Then normalize only known formatting noise.

00:00:09.322 --> 00:00:13.857
If the string contains meaningful structure, parse the pieces you need.

00:00:13.857 --> 00:00:19.717
Validation is a separate step that asks whether the cleaned value follows an expected rule.

00:00:19.717 --> 00:00:24.092
Finally, use the cleaned field for analysis or reporting.

00:00:24.092 --> 00:00:28.857
When traceability matters, preserve the raw source value as well.

00:00:28.857 --> 00:00:33.097
Text cleaning should separate normalization from interpretation.

00:00:33.097 --> 00:00:38.297
Trimming spaces or standardizing case is usually safe when the rule is documented;

00:00:38.297 --> 00:00:43.947
correcting a person's name or guessing an email address is a much stronger intervention.

00:00:43.947 --> 00:00:47.256
Preserve the original value when auditability matters.
